## Important Product Objects and Concepts

### Transactional message

A system-triggered email or SMS sent to one specific person because of an action, event, status, or security need.

### Transactional email

A critical email such as an order confirmation, password reset, appointment reminder, shipping update, or account alert.

### Transactional SMS

A critical SMS such as an authentication code, login code, security alert, reminder, or urgent service update.

### Source

A connected sending system such as a webshop, application, CRM, platform, or internal tool.

### Flow

A structured transactional scenario that determines how a message is triggered, which channel is used, and which template applies.

### Trigger

A system event that initiates a transactional message, such as an order, login, password reset, status change, or delivery update.

### API

A connection method used by applications and platforms to trigger transactional emails or SMS directly.

### SMTP

A connection method used by existing systems to send email through SendPro.

### Webhook

A real-time event update sent from SendPro back to another system, often for delivery status, monitoring, or troubleshooting.

### Template

A reusable structure for transactional email content.

### HTML template

A template built with HTML, often used for structured and branded transactional emails.

### Freemarker

The template engine used to generate dynamic and personalised email content based on data from source systems.

### Variable

A placeholder in a template that is filled with data from the source system.

### Conditional content

Template logic that changes content depending on data or situation.

### Nested loop

Template logic that repeats content structures, such as order lines or item lists.

### Quick editor

A visual editor for adjusting simpler templates, text, images, and variables without editing HTML or code.

### Message type

The category of transactional message, such as order confirmation, password reset, security alert, or shipping update.

### Delivery status

The current state of a sent message, such as sent, delivered, failed, bounced, delayed, or opened where available.

### Delivery report

A report showing delivery and performance data for transactional messages.

### SLA

A Service Level Agreement describing platform availability, performance, and support commitments.

### Premium SLA

An enhanced SLA option for organisations with higher reliability and support requirements.

### Emergency line

A 24/7 support line for core feature outages in enterprise scenarios.

